WEBVTT

00:14.139 --> 00:15.557
Keep going.

00:15.640 --> 00:18.893
- Back!
- Which one are you talking about, Weather?

00:19.728 --> 00:22.731
Is it Jolyne, who you think
is already near the hospital?

00:22.814 --> 00:25.734
Or… do you mean the priest is nearby?

00:25.817 --> 00:28.987
No, it's all three, Anastasia.

00:29.070 --> 00:31.948
Jolyne, the priest, and another enemy.

00:32.532 --> 00:33.867
I feel all three of them.

00:33.950 --> 00:36.286
Find them. Where are they?

00:36.369 --> 00:38.288
Are they inside the building?

00:40.707 --> 00:42.083
Attention all passengers.

00:42.167 --> 00:49.174
It is July 21, 2005,
and time to destination is 21:33.

00:49.257 --> 00:51.134
This aircraft will crash to the ground.

00:52.802 --> 00:54.929
TWO MINUTES UNTIL CRASH

00:56.765 --> 00:58.933
What the hell are you doing?

00:59.017 --> 01:01.144
Why are you messing with that door?

01:01.227 --> 01:03.730
We can't find the exit on the ceiling.

01:03.813 --> 01:08.151
The fastest way to get out
is to defeat the Stand User.

01:09.486 --> 01:11.905
Ermes, hold onto my thread again.

01:11.988 --> 01:13.907
Grab onto to a fixture.

01:13.990 --> 01:15.658
You, flight attendant,

01:15.742 --> 01:18.369
go change the door to manual mode.

01:18.453 --> 01:20.371
What? Hold on.

01:20.455 --> 01:24.375
Isn't it dangerous to open
the door mid-flight?

01:24.459 --> 01:25.502
Doesn't the air pressure…

01:30.131 --> 01:31.424
No.

01:32.008 --> 01:33.510
Go!

01:33.593 --> 01:36.805
She's riding the airflow
to strike the User!

01:44.062 --> 01:45.438
Mayday!

01:45.522 --> 01:48.149
Took a hit from a MiG.

01:48.233 --> 01:49.526
Lost control of the aircraft.

01:50.109 --> 01:52.278
This is coming to a close fast.

01:52.362 --> 01:54.948
Who are you?

01:55.490 --> 01:59.202
Doesn't matter.
Looks like the back seat was compromised.

01:59.285 --> 02:01.913
Check the damage for me, will you?

02:01.996 --> 02:03.039
What's this?

02:14.968 --> 02:16.970
Fuck!

02:17.679 --> 02:19.139
Jolyne!

02:19.722 --> 02:21.349
Stone Ocean!

02:23.268 --> 02:25.103
McCoy on the line.

02:25.186 --> 02:26.813
We just arrived at the scene.

02:27.355 --> 02:31.109
This is incomprehensible,
but there's a hole in a patient's room.

02:31.192 --> 02:32.443
Its depth is unknown.

02:34.195 --> 02:37.532
Jolyne Cujoh learned how to fight
in prison.

02:38.116 --> 02:42.328
She foresaw that
her launched attack would fail.

02:42.412 --> 02:44.998
She left the plane for the walkie-talkie.

02:45.081 --> 02:47.584
She waited for the police
to arrive at the scene.

02:47.667 --> 02:50.962
She knew the officers would bring radios.

02:51.045 --> 02:53.131
She will call her ally now.

02:53.214 --> 02:57.051
The frequency on those talkies
can be adjusted to dial cell phones.

02:57.135 --> 02:59.846
Can't you just shut up for a moment?

02:59.929 --> 03:02.223
Does it look like I'm losing?

03:02.307 --> 03:07.103
Tell me, Father. Who's winning?

04:39.946 --> 04:43.199
I grew up not knowing who my father was.

04:43.783 --> 04:48.871
I got sick of my mother and stepfather
who doted on my stepsisters,

04:48.955 --> 04:50.456
so I ran away from home.

04:50.540 --> 04:51.666
I was 13.

04:52.667 --> 04:54.836
I meant to be gone for a few days,

04:54.919 --> 04:57.672
and I was wandering around,
looking for a place to sleep.

04:57.755 --> 05:00.008
Just then, a pair of spikes
fell from the skies.

05:01.134 --> 05:02.468
They were baseball spikes.

05:03.052 --> 05:05.013
They smelled very nice.

05:05.805 --> 05:08.391
Did someone toss them from a roof?

05:08.474 --> 05:10.435
It made no sense.
The spikes were brand new.

05:10.518 --> 05:12.979
They were sized 28.5cm.

05:13.563 --> 05:15.648
They were too big for my feet,

05:15.732 --> 05:18.776
but I liked the satisfying sounds
they made.

05:18.860 --> 05:21.070
I walked down the street cheerfully.

05:21.904 --> 05:24.282
That's when the cops pulled over
and arrested me.

05:26.451 --> 05:29.037
This is not a trial.

05:29.120 --> 05:31.080
We have questions for you.

05:31.164 --> 05:32.206
Okay?

05:32.832 --> 05:35.501
Did you steal them?

05:36.085 --> 05:39.464
The shoes were signed
by the baseball player Ichiro.

05:39.547 --> 05:43.092
The pair was originally donated
to children with disabilities.

05:43.718 --> 05:47.388
The collectors would pay
up to 10,000 dollars for them.

05:47.472 --> 05:50.308
The theft was all over the news.

05:50.391 --> 05:52.477
I told her the truth.

05:53.061 --> 05:54.771
They fell from the sky.

05:54.854 --> 05:58.775
You should be ashamed of yourself,
stealing from children with disabilities!

05:58.858 --> 06:03.154
Go reflect on your actions
in juvenile detention!

06:03.988 --> 06:08.451
This judge sent me to juvenile detention
based solely on circumstantial evidence!

06:08.534 --> 06:10.703
My parents did not appeal the case.

06:11.537 --> 06:12.705
Four months later,

06:12.789 --> 06:15.208
the actual thief confessed.

06:15.291 --> 06:17.752
He feared Ichiro's spikes
would get traced.

06:17.835 --> 06:20.254
So he tossed them
down a ventilation shaft,

06:20.338 --> 06:22.924
and somehow the spikes fell onto my head.

06:25.051 --> 06:28.012
By the time my innocence was proven,

06:28.096 --> 06:30.223
my body and soul was already hurt.

06:30.932 --> 06:33.684
I couldn't even walk straight.

06:33.768 --> 06:36.437
Somehow, there was a hole
in the facility courtyard.

06:36.521 --> 06:38.815
I tripped on it and fell.

06:38.898 --> 06:43.486
There was a knife inside a plastic bag
buried in the ground.

06:43.569 --> 06:44.904
I stabbed my hand on it.

06:45.488 --> 06:47.740
You've done it now.

06:47.824 --> 06:50.701
I was hiding that knife, dammit.

06:50.785 --> 06:53.246
The next day, a gang henchman
who was three years older than I,

06:53.329 --> 06:56.457
beat the life out of me.

06:56.541 --> 06:58.584
A doctor treated my wounds.

06:58.668 --> 07:01.170
Yet two weeks later,

07:01.254 --> 07:03.589
bloody pus and a worm gushed out.

07:03.673 --> 07:06.425
I also almost died from a terrible fever.

07:07.260 --> 07:09.053
Since that day,

07:09.137 --> 07:13.057
I hid from society
and started to live a tiresome life.

07:13.641 --> 07:16.018
One time, I pissed next to a trash bin.

07:16.102 --> 07:18.229
The walls crumbled down,

07:18.312 --> 07:21.566
and a woman's skull showed itself
from the walls.

07:21.649 --> 07:23.609
And now,

07:23.693 --> 07:28.072
I finally understand
the cause of my bizarre life.

07:28.739 --> 07:31.701
It was my ability, Netherworld!

07:32.577 --> 07:36.038
Yes, at last,
my ability is under control, 

07:36.122 --> 07:40.126
but does this mean
I'm indebted to Father Pucchi?

07:40.751 --> 07:41.586
No.

07:42.378 --> 07:46.299
My father Dio's blood
runs through my veins.

07:46.883 --> 07:47.842
Father Pucchi,

07:47.925 --> 07:50.720
what makes you so much better than me?

07:51.304 --> 07:54.724
I can throw you into that plane.

07:55.349 --> 07:59.061
I haven't had a single slip-up.
Not even one!

07:59.145 --> 08:02.899
He rams through with his decisions,
just like that old hag of a judge.

08:02.982 --> 08:06.027
I'm getting really pissed at him.

08:07.361 --> 08:09.989
I, Versus, am invincible.

08:10.072 --> 08:12.742
Nothing is impossible with Netherworld!

08:20.458 --> 08:22.960
What makes him so special?

08:23.044 --> 08:26.339
What if I present myself instead of him
on the new moon?

08:27.215 --> 08:31.302
Can I inherit the power
Dio hoped to obtain?

08:31.385 --> 08:33.137
I have the right too.

08:33.221 --> 08:35.306
I'm Dio's son!

08:38.684 --> 08:40.811
It's Weather Forecast's memory disc.

08:41.437 --> 08:45.024
How can I use this to my advantage?

08:45.107 --> 08:48.694
I want the power to go to heaven.

08:48.778 --> 08:50.905
Jolyne!

08:54.450 --> 08:56.452
Emporio, pick up the phone!

08:56.536 --> 08:58.079
Emporio!

08:58.162 --> 09:01.082
Hey you!
Tell me the model of this fighter jet!

09:01.165 --> 09:03.251
How do I eject?

09:03.334 --> 09:05.920
The seat must be able to eject somehow!

09:06.003 --> 09:07.797
I've seen it in movies.

09:07.880 --> 09:10.258
Tell me how to eject the seat!

09:10.341 --> 09:12.885
There's an ejection lever on the seat.

09:12.969 --> 09:16.180
But I didn't eject, you see.

09:16.764 --> 09:19.475
This jet crashed to the ground
before I could escape.

09:19.559 --> 09:21.143
Those are the facts.

09:21.769 --> 09:24.313
No one can escape this aircraft.

09:24.397 --> 09:27.316
Pulling the lever won't do a thing.

09:28.901 --> 09:30.486
What's wrong, Jolyne?

09:30.570 --> 09:32.446
It hasn't been that long.

09:32.530 --> 09:34.407
Emporio!

09:34.490 --> 09:36.450
I'm inside a hole at the hospital.

09:36.534 --> 09:38.953
Ermes is on a commercial plane
that crashed years ago.

09:39.036 --> 09:42.039
I'm on a fighter jet.
We're about to crash!

09:42.123 --> 09:44.292
Search for ways to help us!

09:45.084 --> 09:46.085
What?

09:47.878 --> 09:49.130
Father Pucchi,

09:49.213 --> 09:51.382
do you have any use for Jolyne's body?

09:51.465 --> 09:55.595
The fighter jet pilot's body
was never fully recovered.

09:56.304 --> 09:58.764
The impact obliterated him.

09:59.348 --> 10:02.101
Hello? Jolyne, take a deep breath.

10:02.184 --> 10:04.186
I can't tell what's going on.

10:04.270 --> 10:06.105
I'll head back to the hospital now.

10:06.188 --> 10:07.732
No, Emporio.

10:07.815 --> 10:09.734
I'm stuck in the memory of the past!

10:09.817 --> 10:11.611
We can't change the crash.

10:11.694 --> 10:15.323
My survival depends on getting out,
but I can't eject!

10:15.406 --> 10:18.534
No, we're out of time.

10:18.618 --> 10:20.244
There's less than a minute left.

10:20.328 --> 10:23.956
The fighter jet will crash
before this plane!

10:31.088 --> 10:33.132
You flew the fighter jet into…

10:33.215 --> 10:34.634
You're right, Emporio.

10:34.717 --> 10:37.470
It didn't explode, Emporio.

10:37.553 --> 10:40.306
I rammed it into the commercial plane,
but it didn't explode!

10:40.389 --> 10:42.183
Of course, it didn't.

10:42.266 --> 10:44.310
The fact is that the planes crashed.

10:44.393 --> 10:46.187
So the planes will eventually crash.

10:46.270 --> 10:50.149
Until then, they won't explode
no matter what you do.

10:50.232 --> 10:52.526
- Jolyne!
- I'm back!

10:52.610 --> 10:55.529
Emporio, what should I do next?

10:55.613 --> 10:57.073
Let me see.

10:57.740 --> 11:01.994
It's Flight 2882 to Dallas,
a crash incident from six years ago.

11:02.078 --> 11:04.246
Miraculously, two passengers survived.

11:04.330 --> 11:07.124
I'm looking it up on my ghost computer.

11:07.208 --> 11:09.126
Go find those two seats!

11:09.210 --> 11:11.754
You may not be able to leave the aircraft,

11:11.837 --> 11:13.964
but the ability runs
the exact course of events.

11:14.048 --> 11:16.592
You can survive by sitting in those seats.

11:16.676 --> 11:19.553
Emporio, hurry and find out
the seat numbers!

11:20.137 --> 11:22.390
That's Jolyne Cujoh.

11:22.473 --> 11:25.643
She forges her own paths.

11:25.726 --> 11:30.189
Do you still think
you can finish her off, Versus?

11:30.272 --> 11:31.982
Shut up!

11:32.066 --> 11:34.985
Who does he think he is?

11:37.696 --> 11:39.031
Found it, Jolyne!

11:39.115 --> 11:42.701
A newspaper article published
the seat numbers of the two survivors.

11:43.285 --> 11:47.415
They're Economy class, 51D and 51F.

11:47.498 --> 11:48.833
It's at the very rear.

11:48.916 --> 11:52.711
It also says that
the plane crashed at 21:33.

11:52.795 --> 11:53.629
It's all true!

11:53.712 --> 11:54.839
Run, Jolyne!

11:55.589 --> 11:57.675
The enemy Stand is here!

11:57.758 --> 12:01.929
It wants to get ahead of us
and destroy the seats!

12:02.012 --> 12:05.516
Thirty-two seconds left until impact.
This is a minor setback.

12:06.725 --> 12:08.727
I only have to destroy the seats.

12:09.353 --> 12:11.439
That's all it takes
to obliterate the fact.

12:14.942 --> 12:15.776
Ermes!

12:15.860 --> 12:17.403
Secure the seats!

12:17.486 --> 12:20.781
We only have to sit in those seats
and survive the crash.

12:20.865 --> 12:23.075
Then, we can face the Stand User!

12:23.159 --> 12:24.535
Let's make it out of this alive

12:24.618 --> 12:27.246
and defeat the Stand User!

12:28.372 --> 12:31.417
The seats are still intact,
but their attempt is futile.

12:31.500 --> 12:33.836
There's only 21 seconds left.

12:33.919 --> 12:35.421
I'll say this again.

12:35.504 --> 12:39.008
The only safe seats are 51D and 51F.

12:39.091 --> 12:41.302
Don't sit anywhere else!

12:41.385 --> 12:42.887
According to the article,

12:42.970 --> 12:46.056
all other seats were destroyed
in an explosion on impact.

12:46.140 --> 12:50.311
It was a fluke caused
under miraculous circumstances.

12:50.394 --> 12:51.812
The two seats were in an air pocket.

12:51.896 --> 12:54.940
Once you sit down, buckle up.

12:55.024 --> 12:58.110
Guard yourselves with your Stands,
or you won't survive!

13:02.239 --> 13:04.700
Move! I'm taking this seat!

13:04.783 --> 13:06.911
What are you doing--

13:06.994 --> 13:09.079
Shut up and scram!

13:09.163 --> 13:11.040
You are nothing but recorded facts.

13:11.123 --> 13:12.500
No more than memories of survivors!

13:13.083 --> 13:15.461
You're not the people nor their souls.

13:15.544 --> 13:18.214
The real old man is alive and happy.

13:18.297 --> 13:20.799
Get out of my way.
Jolyne, we don't have time.

13:20.883 --> 13:23.052
Let's buckle up--

13:35.022 --> 13:36.982
Move, brat!

13:37.066 --> 13:38.776
You're in our seat!

13:38.859 --> 13:40.319
Hold on, Ermes.

13:48.827 --> 13:52.540
Where the hell did you come from?

13:52.623 --> 13:54.792
This isn't my room.

13:55.292 --> 13:56.669
Where am I?

13:56.752 --> 14:00.297
I'm supposed to take my medication
after my nap.

14:00.381 --> 14:02.258
You came down from the ceiling!

14:02.341 --> 14:05.261
Don't tell me you're…

14:05.344 --> 14:06.845
This can't be!

14:06.929 --> 14:10.140
They're not illusions, or even passengers!

14:10.224 --> 14:13.185
Where's the nurse?

14:15.312 --> 14:17.189
She's a real girl!

14:17.273 --> 14:22.319
The asshole pushed these kids
down the hole!

14:24.113 --> 14:25.531
What?

14:26.198 --> 14:28.576
No need to destroy the seats.

14:28.659 --> 14:29.952
Jolyne Cujoh.

14:30.035 --> 14:32.496
Don't forget to buckle up.

14:32.580 --> 14:36.083
Go on, push them out of the way
and take a seat.

14:36.166 --> 14:38.919
That way, you two will survive.

14:39.003 --> 14:41.046
Physically speaking, that is.

14:41.797 --> 14:45.050
Once you crawl out of that plane alive,

14:45.134 --> 14:48.345
you won't be able to bear the guilt.

14:48.429 --> 14:52.433
Guilt that you sacrificed children's lives
to save your own.

14:53.142 --> 14:58.022
Will you be able to fight me
with so much guilt on your shoulders?

14:58.522 --> 15:01.901
You won't be so cocky then.

15:03.819 --> 15:07.948
Netherworld may not be
suitable for combat,

15:08.532 --> 15:13.120
but it can deal enough damage
to finish off such guilt-ridden fools.

15:13.203 --> 15:16.582
Jolyne? What's going on? Hello?

15:16.665 --> 15:19.543
What's happening? Who are you talking to?

15:19.627 --> 15:23.547
Dammit, the plane is beginning to shake!

15:23.631 --> 15:25.549
We'll put each child in our laps.

15:25.633 --> 15:29.345
No, we'll all die.
Each seat can only fit one person!

15:29.428 --> 15:32.181
And there are three children!

15:32.890 --> 15:35.184
Are we in your seats?

15:35.267 --> 15:38.479
It takes me a second to stand up.

15:38.562 --> 15:41.899
Sorry, we'll get out of your way.
You can have your seat back.

15:45.694 --> 15:48.489
It's time. Two seconds,

15:48.572 --> 15:51.367
one second, brace for impact.

15:52.117 --> 15:54.495
Jolyne!

16:04.213 --> 16:05.923
STAND NAME: SMACK
STAND MASTER: ERMES COSTELLO

16:19.687 --> 16:22.481
The victory is yours, Versus.

16:23.065 --> 16:25.526
But I saw three children.

16:25.609 --> 16:27.611
That's one too many.

16:27.695 --> 16:29.947
Don't you feel guilty?

16:30.030 --> 16:33.409
No, it wasn't my fault.

16:33.993 --> 16:37.246
I was forced to do this
because Jolyne called her ally.

16:37.746 --> 16:40.416
Jolyne kept resisting
by finding the survivors' seats.

16:40.958 --> 16:43.961
Not to mention, I did this for you,

16:44.586 --> 16:46.088
Father Pucchi.

16:47.464 --> 16:49.299
Look, Versus.

16:56.223 --> 16:59.435
That's Ermes's sticker.

17:06.900 --> 17:08.819
The surviving old man.

17:09.319 --> 17:14.074
The fact of the matter is
that the survivors didn't die.

17:14.158 --> 17:16.285
That's Ermes's sticker.

17:17.036 --> 17:18.245
She copied the survivors

17:18.328 --> 17:21.206
and kept the children safe
inside their bodies.

17:23.292 --> 17:25.669
Ermes! That means…

17:26.378 --> 17:30.090
Where is Jolyne Cujoh?

17:31.341 --> 17:32.760
Ermes!

17:35.471 --> 17:37.097
Ermes!

17:37.931 --> 17:40.559
She lodged herself
in the body of the other survivor!

17:41.143 --> 17:44.063
Dammit, Ermes!

17:44.146 --> 17:46.607
But Jolyne is dead!

17:46.690 --> 17:49.693
Jolyne has nowhere to turn!

17:50.277 --> 17:51.904
If I were you,

17:51.987 --> 17:54.865
I'd think this through more carefully.

17:54.948 --> 17:57.951
Asshole, whose side are you on--

18:13.258 --> 18:16.762
Jolyne unraveled her body into threads
as much as she could.

18:16.845 --> 18:21.308
She then hid inside my body,
surviving the crash.

18:21.391 --> 18:23.227
Good grief.

18:24.561 --> 18:27.940
Jolyne Cujoh isn't filled with guilt,

18:28.023 --> 18:32.361
but rather coming at you,
burning with wrathful justice.

18:32.444 --> 18:34.446
What will you do now, Versus?

18:35.989 --> 18:37.741
Netherworld!

18:47.292 --> 18:49.586
You won't be digging a hole

18:49.670 --> 18:52.089
or excavating memories any longer.

18:52.172 --> 18:54.550
You're finally ours,

18:54.633 --> 18:56.593
Father Pucchi!

18:56.677 --> 18:59.471
Can I finish off the priest?

18:59.555 --> 19:02.057
Or should we do this together?

19:02.891 --> 19:06.520
Unfortunately, Versus,
it looks like you lost.

19:06.603 --> 19:09.314
Jolyne Cujoh's gravitational pull to me

19:09.398 --> 19:11.984
was much stronger than yours.

19:14.570 --> 19:16.280
Let's finish him off, Jolyne!

19:16.363 --> 19:19.867
This groundhog is done for!

19:20.742 --> 19:24.413
Weather Forecast!

19:30.669 --> 19:33.505
What the hell? What did he just do?

19:33.589 --> 19:35.924
Jolyne, finish him off!

19:37.551 --> 19:38.677
When did you take it from me?

19:38.760 --> 19:41.471
Was it when Jolyne blasted you?

19:41.555 --> 19:43.015
Give it back immediately.

19:43.098 --> 19:44.766
It belongs to me.

19:44.850 --> 19:47.936
You don't understand what you're doing.

19:48.020 --> 19:50.480
Sorry, but I'm not going to die here,

19:50.564 --> 19:51.648
Father Pucchi.

19:52.649 --> 19:56.486
My ability finally awakened.

19:56.570 --> 20:00.699
I've never had anything to live up to.

20:00.782 --> 20:04.453
I'm finally starting to understand
why I was born.

20:04.536 --> 20:07.456
You don't understand anything.

20:07.539 --> 20:10.876
His memory must stay with me,

20:10.959 --> 20:12.502
at least for another three days.

20:12.586 --> 20:14.796
I won't end here!

20:14.880 --> 20:17.424
I have the right to become happy!

20:17.507 --> 20:18.926
What are you saying?

20:19.009 --> 20:20.928
What are you guys talking about?

20:21.011 --> 20:22.137
Jolyne,

20:22.221 --> 20:24.431
finish him off already!

20:24.514 --> 20:26.350
It's too late.

20:26.433 --> 20:28.644
You can't finish me.

20:28.727 --> 20:30.896
He will regain his memory.

20:30.979 --> 20:33.273
I know it because I read his memory.

20:33.857 --> 20:37.486
He's not the ally you think he is.

20:37.569 --> 20:38.695
Memory?

20:38.779 --> 20:40.614
Is he talking about Weather Forecast?

20:40.697 --> 20:42.574
Did he throw Weather's disc?

20:43.158 --> 20:49.331
Weather Forecast is more than
a convict with amnesia.

20:50.040 --> 20:53.669
He doesn't remember how his ability works.

20:53.752 --> 20:58.382
His brother, Father Pucchi,
sealed away his demonic powers!

21:00.133 --> 21:03.136
He is the priest's younger brother.

21:03.220 --> 21:06.390
So Rikiel was telling the truth,
they really are…

21:06.473 --> 21:08.475
Weather Forecast and Father Pucchi?

21:09.101 --> 21:10.769
So you used Netherworld

21:10.852 --> 21:14.022
to read the disc's recorded facts.

21:14.106 --> 21:17.776
Versus!
You are nothing but a thatched hut.

21:17.859 --> 21:22.322
You have no place in the grand purpose
Dio and I have fought for!

21:23.031 --> 21:25.826
He's starting to remember.

21:25.909 --> 21:27.536
Look, he's here.

21:30.247 --> 21:34.167
Rainbows. There are rainbows!
The devil's rainbows!

21:34.251 --> 21:35.794
It's Heavy Forecast!

21:37.004 --> 21:39.381
Weather, what's the matter?

21:39.464 --> 21:42.092
Where's Jolyne? Why are you crouching?

21:46.096 --> 21:48.307
Weather, what's wrong?

21:48.390 --> 21:49.474
What are you doing?

21:54.813 --> 21:57.941
What's your problem, punk?

21:58.025 --> 21:59.609
I was sitting here first.

21:59.693 --> 22:03.447
Don't touch me, I'll kill you!

22:10.537 --> 22:14.875
THREE MORE DAYS UNTIL THE NEW MOON

23:41.294 --> 23:46.299
Subtitle translation by: Megumi Hunter
